<title>HONG KONG: CIBC sets warrants on Taiwan closed-end fund index.</title>
<headline>CIBC sets warrants on Taiwan closed-end fund index.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Imperial Bank of Commerce said it issued on Friday 20 million American-style call warrants on an equally weighted index of Taiwan closed-end funds.</p>
<p>The index comprises of:</p>
<p>Kwang Hua Growth Fund</p>
<p>NITC Fu-Yuan Fund</p>
<p>Citizen Fund</p>
<p>China Success Fund</p>
<p>President Mutual Fund</p>
<p>Masterlink Mutual Fund</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE    US$2.5397     PREMIUM	   12.00 PCT</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE     US$0.304764   GEARING	   8.33 X</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	16.JUL.97     EXER LOT	  5,000</p>
<p> LISTING	   LUXEMBOURG    GOVERNING LAW   ENGLISH</p>
<p> INITIAL INDEX VALUE   US$2.5397</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
</text>
